    :BulkCarrier rdfs:subClassOf :Vessel ; rdfs:comment "Bulk carrier means a ship which is constructed generally with single deck, top-side tanks and hopper side tanks in cargo spaces, and is intended primarily to carry dry cargo in bulk, and includes such types as ore carriers and combination carriers. (SOLAS IX/1.6). Bulk carrier means a ship which is intended primarily to carry dry cargo in bulk, including such types as ore carriers and combination carriers. (SOLAS XII/1.1)" .
    :Bulk_Carrier rdfs:subClassOf :Cargo_Vessel .
    :Bulk_Carrier_With_Vehicle_Deck rdfs:subClassOf :Cargo_Vessel .
    :Bulk_Storage_Barge rdfs:subClassOf :Cargo_Vessel .
    :Bulker rdfs:subClassOf :Cargo_Vessel .
    :Bunker rdfs:subClassOf :Vessel ;
        rdfs:comment "A bunker is generally applied to the storage of petroleum products in tanks, and the practice and business of refueling ships. Bunkering operations are located at seaports, and they include the storage of bunker (ship) fuels and the provision of the fuel to vessels. Bunkering includes the shipboard logistics of loading fuel and distributing it among available bunkers (on-board fuel tanks)." .
    
    :Bunkering_Tanker rdfs:subClassOf :Tanker .
